WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:05.468
Agent states are the reasons an agent gives when they are not taking work:

00:00:05.468 --> 00:00:07.311
lunch, a meeting, training.

00:00:07.311 --> 00:00:11.277
This video shows why they exist, how to create a reason code, and

00:00:11.277 --> 00:00:13.790
what agents see in their presence menu.

00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:22.241
When agents are not taking work, a manager needs to know why.

00:00:22.241 --> 00:00:25.576
An agent at lunch is not the same as an agent who is

00:00:25.576 --> 00:00:27.530
stuck with a system problem.

00:00:28.280 --> 00:00:32.236
A reason code gives the agent a name to pick, such as Lunch,

00:00:32.236 --> 00:00:34.094
Team meeting or Training.

00:00:34.094 --> 00:00:37.810
Each one belongs to one of the built-in presence states.

00:00:38.560 --> 00:00:42.573
Reports and the Live dashboard then show both the state and the reason,

00:00:42.573 --> 00:00:43.980
so nobody has to ask.

00:00:48.180 --> 00:00:52.754
A reason code has a name, and the state it applies to:

00:00:52.754 --> 00:00:58.930
Break, Away, Do not disturb, Meeting, Training, or After-hours unavailable.

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:03.419
A sort order decides where it appears in the presence menu.

00:01:03.419 --> 00:01:05.490
A lower number appears higher.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.071
The site starts with seven reason codes.

00:01:09.071 --> 00:01:12.580
You can change them, delete them, and add your own.

00:01:16.800 --> 00:01:20.501
Open Interaction Center, Management, Agent states.

00:01:20.501 --> 00:01:24.930
The list shows each reason code with the state it applies to.

00:01:24.930 --> 00:01:26.780
Click Add reason code.

00:01:27.236 --> 00:01:31.896
Type a Name, such as Customer visit, and an optional Description.

00:01:32.346 --> 00:01:34.486
Choose the state it Applies to.

00:01:34.486 --> 00:01:37.146
A visit away from the desk is a Meeting.

00:01:37.605 --> 00:01:39.097
Set a Sort order.

00:01:39.097 --> 00:01:42.665
Lower numbers appear higher in the presence menu.

00:01:42.665 --> 00:01:45.455
Leave Enabled ticked, and click Save.

00:01:49.663 --> 00:01:54.176
Agents change their state from the presence menu on My workspace.

00:01:54.176 --> 00:01:59.453
The same menu is in the Contact Center bar at the bottom of every admin page.

00:01:59.904 --> 00:02:01.876
Available is always listed.

00:02:01.876 --> 00:02:05.762
Every reason code that is not a break is listed on its own,

00:02:05.762 --> 00:02:07.914
and sets the state right away.

00:02:07.914 --> 00:02:10.484
The new Customer visit is among them.

00:02:10.947 --> 00:02:15.577
Break reasons are grouped under a Break heading, here Short break and Lunch.

00:02:19.796 --> 00:02:25.076
To stop offering a reason, open it and untick Enabled, then click Save.

00:02:28.379 --> 00:02:32.923
A disabled reason code is hidden from the presence menu, but it stays

00:02:32.923 --> 00:02:36.679
on historical records, so past reports still make sense.

00:02:40.879 --> 00:02:45.644
When an agent is busy on a call, the Break heading reads Request break.

00:02:45.644 --> 00:02:49.109
The break starts as soon as the current work ends.

00:02:49.859 --> 00:02:55.322
If no reason codes exist at all, the menu falls back to the plain states:

00:02:55.322 --> 00:03:00.439
Away, Do not disturb, Meeting, Training and After-hours unavailable.

00:03:01.189 --> 00:03:06.102
The starting codes are Short break and Lunch, Away from desk, Team meeting,

00:03:06.102 --> 00:03:08.649
Coaching, Training and System issue.

00:03:12.849 --> 00:03:17.909
Separating lunch from short breaks, so reports show the real length of each.

00:03:18.659 --> 00:03:24.759
A Coaching code, so supervisors know an agent is in a review and not idle.

00:03:25.509 --> 00:03:30.189
A System issue code, to see how much time a tooling problem costs.

00:03:30.939 --> 00:03:36.219
A code for after-hours unavailability, for agents who work a split shift.

00:03:38.219 --> 00:03:43.113
Create the reasons your team needs, and agents pick one when they step away.

00:03:43.113 --> 00:03:45.858
Reports and the dashboard show the rest.

00:03:45.858 --> 00:03:47.409
Thanks for watching.

